# Identity patterns for docker/scan-image.sh. Copy to docker/scan-identity and fill in.
#
# docker/scan-identity is gitignored on purpose: it holds the strings that identify you, and
# committing them would publish exactly what the scanner exists to keep out of an image.
#
# Sourced as shell, so these are extended-regex alternations in single quotes.

# Strings that must never appear ANYWHERE in a published image. Scanned over every byte.
# Your registry handle, your username, your home directory, your mail address.
IDENTITY='myhandle|/home/myuser'

# Weaker signals: real when they appear in files the build wrote, noise in third-party
# packages. Scanned only in authored paths. Your real name, your mail domain, forge URLs.
WEAK='firstname|lastname|example\.com|github\.com/myhandle'
